Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 06/29/2023]
1.  Er >= 232 keV: weighted average of Buchmann et al. 1983 and Vogelaar 1989 [PhD thesis]. 
2.  Er = 190 keV: weighted average of Vogelaar [PhD thesis] and Ruiz et al. 2006.
3.  Er = 128 keV: we used 27Al(d,p) result of Magerin et al. 2015/Lotay et al. 2020. This assumes the mirror assignments of Lotay et al. 2011 are correct.
4.  Er = 95 keV: this level has been reported in some studies, but not in others. It has not been adopted in ENSDF. Upper limit estimated assuming C2S=1. 
5.  Er = 70 keV: we used SM result of Tab. 1 in Lotay et al. 2020 [assumed uncertainty in C2S of factor 5]; this assumes the mirror assignments of Lotay et al. 2011 
    are correct.
6.  Er = 7 keV: upper limit obtained assuming C2S=1.
7.  DC estimated using weighted average of C2S from shell model and (d,p) mirror measurement; these values are listed in Tab. 1 of Lotay et al. 2020.

   
